  "body": "Start building immediately. No waiting. No uncertainty.\r\nUnlock the full potential of this exceptional 8-terrace-home development site at 17A Arklow Lane, Stanmore Bay — a rare opportunity where all the hard work has already been done.\r\nWith Resource Consent, Building Consent, and Engineering Plan Approval already granted, this project is truly ready to commence construction straight away.\r\n\r\nWhy Developers Will Love 17A Arklow Lane\r\n• Fully Approved – Build with Confidence\r\n• Resource Consent issued\r\n• Building Consent issued\r\n• EPA (Engineering Plan Approval) completed\r\n• A genuine turnkey, shovel-ready project — no delays, no holding costs, just action.\r\n\r\nPrime Stanmore Bay Location\r\nPositioned in the heart of one of the Hibiscus Coast’s fastest-growing suburbs, just minutes to:\r\n• Beautiful beaches\r\n• Schools and local amenities\r\n• Shopping and transport links\r\n\r\nPenlink Infrastructure Boost\r\nBenefit from the transformational Penlink project, connecting Stanmore Bay directly to SH1 — cutting travel time and enhancing long-term value.\r\nHigh-Growth Mixed Use Zoning\r\nSet on a generous 867m² freehold Mixed Use site, offering flexibility and strong future upside in a booming development corridor.\r\n\r\nApproved Townhouse Scheme – 8 Terrace Homes\r\n• Lots 1–6: 2-bedroom + study, 1.5-bathroom terrace homes with car park (approx. 75.23m² each)\r\n• Lots 7–8: 2-bedroom, 1.5-bathroom terrace homes with car park (approx. 73.3m² each)\r\nA modern, efficient layout designed for today’s market demand.\r\n\r\nAct Now – Rare “Ready-to-Go” Site\r\nOpportunities like this are seldom available — a fully consented, build-ready development in a high-demand coastal suburb.\r\nSecure 17A Arklow Lane today and start building immediately.\r\n\r\nPlanning Notice\r\nPlanning: Proposed Plan Change 120 may change planning controls in this area (including natural-hazard and building-height rules). Some hazard provisions have immediate legal effect. Buyers should review the Auckland Council viewer and seek independent legal and planning advice.\r\nBoundary lines shown in the photos are indicative only. Purchasers should refer to the Certificate of Title and seek advice from a registered surveyor for the exact boundary location.",
